    <h2>4. Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      We use carefully selected providers to operate the website, our student
      portal and our communications, including hosting, security, email
      delivery and calendar-based consultation scheduling. Access to student
      and enquiry records is restricted to authorised Waylen staff. These
      providers process information under their own safeguards and
      contractual obligations. We may also share information where required
      by law or when necessary to establish or defend legal claims.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some providers may process information outside the European Economic
      Area. Where this happens, we rely on a lawful transfer mechanism, such
      as an adequacy decision or approved contractual safeguards.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long we keep information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Mailing-list and waitlist details are kept until you unsubscribe, the purpose of the list ends, or after 24 months of inactivity, whichever comes first.</li>
      <li>General enquiries are normally kept for up to 12 months after our last contact.</li>
      <li>Service and transaction records are kept for the period required by Polish accounting, tax and legal rules.</li>
      <li>Security logs are retained only for the period reasonably necessary to investigate abuse and protect the website.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may retain limited information for longer where necessary to comply
      with law, resolve a dispute or record an unsubscribe request.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Cookies and local preferences</h2>
    <p>
      The website stores your session and light/dark theme choice on your
      device, and may remember whether you dismissed an on-site prompt. Our
      hosting and calendar-booking providers may use necessary technologies
      for security, booking and service operation.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Subject to the conditions in data-protection law, you may ask us to
      access, correct, erase or restrict your personal information, provide a
      portable copy, or object to certain processing. You can withdraw
      consent at any time without affecting earlier lawful processing.
      Marketing emails also include an unsubscribe option.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise a right, use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. We
      may need to verify your identity before completing a request. You may
      also lodge a complaint with the President of the Personal Data
      Protection Office in Poland or the data-protection authority in your
      country.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Automated decisions</h2>
    <p>
      Waylen does not use the information collected through this website to
      make decisions based solely on automated means that produce legally
      significant outcomes.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Security and updates</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable organisational and technical measures to protect
      personal information. No online service can guarantee absolute
      security, so please avoid sending sensitive documents through a general
      enquiry form — use your secure student portal instead once your account
      is set up. We may update this policy when our services or providers
      change, and the revision date above will be updated.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For any privacy question, use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>
      or call +48 733 855 863.
    </p>
